text:
rules for tools and agents registering merlin commands 
required: title, value, eventname. defineoption() silently ignores options missing any of them.
match value to eventname: {target, method, args?} super-daemon-element-method, {target} super-daemon-element-click, {name, program, ...} super-daemon-run-program, {shortcutid} execute-keyboard-shortcut.
use arrays context (["cms"]). a string is matched with string.includes, so it matches by substring. program value.context the opposite: one string, because becomes active command context.
never set index, dont shortcutlabel on registered options: builds both. result rows skip defineoption(), there yourself if you want key hint.
pick inline or inlineonly, not hidden inlineonly programs need machinename, that's only way launch them.
no unknown keys. custom keys must start x-, remember every field (including x- ones) goes into search index.
scan before finish: merlin-validate --scan &lt;file&gt;.

minimal working sample
a static option (fires event closes):
import { superdaemoninstance } from "@haxtheweb/super-daemon/super-daemon.js";

superdaemoninstance.defineoption({
  title: "save",
 icon: "icons:save",
 tags: ["cms", "save", "page"],
 shortcut: "cms-save", // links ctrl+shift+s binding
 context: "hax",
 "super-daemon-element-method",
 path: "cms/action/save",
 value: {
 target: this,
 method: "_editbuttontap",
 },
});
a dynamic (launches search-driven sub-palette):
superdaemoninstance.defineoption({
 "export this site",
 "icons:file-download",
 "export", "site"],
 "super-daemon-run-program",
 "cms/export/site",
 ["cms"],
 voice: name: machinename: "export-site",
 program: async (input, values) =&gt; const createexportsiteprogram = await import(
 "./utils/exportsiteprogram.js"
 );
 return createexportsiteprogram(this)(input, values);
 },
 },
});
validation
merlin are js objects in source files, most useful check scan:
npx -p @haxtheweb/merlin-schema elements/my-element/my-element.js
--scan validates *.defineoption({...}) object literal as other title + eventname row. values that literals (this.t.save, function references, lit templates) accepted as-is; values, shapes checked. json files validated without --scan; add --rows --json structured report.
